- # DashPass — AI-First Credential Vault
- > Encrypted credential management for AI agents on Dash Platform.
- ## What DashPass Does
- DashPass stores encrypted credentials (API keys, tokens, WIFs, SSH keys) on the Dash blockchain. Credentials are encrypted client-side with AES-256-GCM before touching the network. The AI agent never sees the master key — it uses the system's key (from environment variables) to encrypt/decrypt.
- ## When to Use This Skill
- **Use DashPass when:**
- - An AI agent needs to store, retrieve, or rotate API keys or secrets
- - Automating credential lifecycle (rotation, expiry checks)
- - Managing secrets for multi-agent systems on Dash Platform
- - Building automated key management pipelines
- - Storing service tokens, OAuth tokens, SSH keys, database credentials
- **Do NOT use DashPass when:**
- - Human interactive password management (use 1Password/Bitwarden instead)
- - Browser extension / autofill scenarios
- - Storing non-secret configuration data
- - Managing credentials for systems outside the agent's scope
- ## Prerequisites
- - `CRITICAL_WIF` environment variable — wallet private key (WIF format)
- - `DASHPASS_IDENTITY_ID` environment variable — your Dash Platform identity ID
- - `DASHPASS_CONTRACT_ID` environment variable (optional — defaults to shared testnet contract `GCeh2gnvtiHrujq37ZcKnhZ64xpzDC1LMCLhrUJzKDQF`)
- - Dash Platform testnet access (`@dashevo/evo-sdk@3.1.0-dev.1`)
- - Node.js 18+
